{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Decide whether the ADR reference gate should also scan src/ for adr/*-slug references, or narrow the RENUMBERING 'fails CI' claim to docs/ only.","criteria":["edge-cases","maintainability"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["scripts/check_adr_numbers.py:156: `for md in sorted(docs_dir.rglob(\"*.md\")):`","scripts/check_adr_numbers.py:176: `docs_dir = adr_dir.parent`","RENUMBERING.md line 36 claims 'a dangling adr/*-slug link fails CI' but src/ refs like src/rebar/schemas/gen_types.py:9 are outside docs/ and are .py, not *.md, so are never scanned."],"finding":"The referential-integrity gate (Rule 7) resolves ADR links only under docs/ (docs_dir defaults to adr_dir.parent = docs/); ADR references in src/ files (e.g. the docstring/comment links rewritten to 0080/0083) are not scanned, so a future stale/renamed ADR reference in source will not fail the gate.","id":"0","impact":0.3,"location":"scripts/check_adr_numbers.py:173","norm_id":"n0d3d4705d838036d","priority":0.3,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["An ADR is renamed later; a src/ comment still points at the old slug — CI stays green while the doc link dangles."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"local","capability_degraded":false,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":true,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":false,"debt_impact":"low","escapes_au